This Terraform program will create an AWS Lex V2 bot for children. The bot will be deployed in the us-west-2 region and will have the following features:

* A custom intent called "help" that will be triggered when a child asks for help
* A custom intent called "play" that will be triggered when a child wants to play a game
* A custom intent called "learn" that will be triggered when a child wants to learn something new
* A custom intent called "tell" that will be triggered when a child wants to tell a story
* A custom intent called "ask" that will be triggered when a child wants to ask a question
* A custom intent called "thank" that will be triggered when a child thanks the bot for its help
* A custom intent called "bye" that will be triggered when a child says goodbye to the bot

The bot will also have the following capabilities:

* The ability to understand natural language and respond to questions and requests in a helpful and engaging way
* The ability to provide information and resources to help children learn and grow
* The ability to play games and engage in fun activities with children
* The ability to tell stories and share information in a way that is both entertaining and informative
* The ability to ask questions and provide answers to help children learn and understand new concepts
* The ability to thank children for their help and support
* The ability to say goodbye to children when they are finished using the bot

The bot will be deployed using the AWS Lex V2 service and will be accessible through the AWS Management Console. The bot will be configured to use the following AWS services:

* AWS Lex V2
* AWS Lambda
* AWS DynamoDB
* AWS S3
* AWS CloudWatch

The bot will also be configured to use the following AWS IAM roles:

* AWSLambdaRole
* AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole
* AWSLambdaVPCAccessExecutionRole
* AWSLambdaDynamoDBExecutionRole
* AWSLambdaS3ExecutionRole
* AWSLambdaCloudWatchExecutionRole

The bot will be deployed using the following Terraform HCL program:
```
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
